SUMMARY:Adult Studio: Papermaking
DESCRIPTION:This 4 hour workshop will introduce the basics of hand papermaking along with a guided tour of the Exhibition. Participants will learn to make several sheets of handmade paper that they can add botanicals to or embellish with pigmented pulps. We will conclude with pressing the handmade sheets so they will be ready to take away at the conclusion of the workshop!  \nGeorgia Deal is a printmaker / papermaker who makes mixed-media works on handmade paper. She is Professor Emeritus and former chair of the Printmaking & Papermaking programs at the Corcoran College of Art & Design in Washington D.C. Currently\, she resides in Asheville\, NC and is the proprietor of Swannanoa Paper\, a collaborative studio that also offers workshops.  \nDeal has taught courses throughout the U.S.\, at Penland School in NC\, Haystack Mtn. School\, ME the Paper & Book Intensive\, Oxbow\, MI\, and abroad in Cortona\, Italy\, Skopelos\, Greece and San Miguel\, Mexico. Her works are in the collections of the Library of Congress\, the Philadelphia Museum of Art\, the Corcoran Gallery of Art\, and Yale Univ. Library amongst others. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/adult-studio-papermaking/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Adult Studio
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/20241105_150141507_iOS-copy-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
